{"name":"Tank","hex":"#5c6141","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tank","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Tank district, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Pakistan.","A district of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Pakistan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tank"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tank","blocks":[{"text":"A tank is an armoured fighting vehicle intended as a primary offensive weapon in front-line ground combat. Tank designs are a balance of heavy firepower, strong armour, and battlefield mobility provided by tracks and a powerful engine; their main armament is often mounted within a turret. They are a mainstay of modern 20th and 21st century ground forces and a key part of combined arms combat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Mark_I_series_tank.jpg/330px-Mark_I_series_tank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tank"},{"title":"Tank (entertainer)","blocks":[{"text":"Durrell Artaze Babbs, better known by his stage name Tank, is an American singer, songwriter, actor, record producer, and podcaster. He began his career as a backing vocalist for Aaliyah and Ginuwine, and signed a recording contract with the former's record label, Blackground Records as a performing act in 1998. His 2001 single, \"Maybe I Deserve\" peaked within the top 40 of the Billboard Hot 100 and led his debut studio album, Force of Nature (2001). It peaked within the top ten of the Billboard 200, while his second album, One Man (2002), peaked within the top 20 and was met with mixed critical reception."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tank-byPhilipRomano.jpg/330px-Tank-byPhilipRomano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tank_(entertainer)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/German_tank_Pz.Kpfw._VI_